-- A door as a state machine: a state and an event make the next state.
-- The states and events are symbols. Known while compiling, the machine
-- runs while compiling, and a transition the table lacks is a compile
-- error: `Locked Open door` is no word `door` for Locked Open.

door: < Closed Open > [ drop drop Opened ] ;
door: < Opened Close > [ drop drop Closed ] ;
door: < Closed Lock > [ drop drop Locked ] ;
door: < Locked Unlock > [ drop drop Closed ] ;

Closed Open door Close door Lock door

-- Symbols are values at run time too. Events read as text become symbols,
-- `"Open" sym!`, as the program runs, and the table is tested then: an
-- event the table lacks for the state stops the program.

"Unlock Open Close" words [ sym! ] map Locked [ door ] fold
